From 03ef2e330ba84fc5e40fe61899c18f4aa713dad9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:35:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(tilelang): cover rank-order reduction tails and strided
 CUDA inputs

Upstream base: local-inference-lab/vllm 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354 plus candidate-38 (1f33102547e4da5c64712390604695d1abd577c4).

Keep the packed BF16 reduction for aligned independent buffers. Replace the CUDA-to-Torch fallback with a strided TileLang reduction, including tails and real numeric dtypes. Normalize tensor metadata to eight dimensions to keep preparation keys independent of model tensor rank. Protect aliased output through a temporary, retain FP32 partials above eight inputs, and reject unsupported GPU contracts explicitly. CPU retains its reference implementation.

Quality: sources are cast to FP32, accumulated in the original rank order and rounded to the output dtype once. The first source is loaded directly to preserve signed zero. No cross-rank transport change. Tests cover independent references, odd sizes, strides, misalignment, mixed types, aliases, dimensions, empty/scalar tensors, CUDA replay and errors. Native results are retained in the deployment experiment. Upstream status: local candidate, not submitted.
